  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For a certain organ pipe, the first three resonance frequencies are in the ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math> respectively. If the frequency of fifth harmonic is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>405</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> and the speed of sound in air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>324</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> the length of the organ pipe is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>405</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>.</p><p>As the first three resonance frequencies are in the ratio of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, therefore it must be a closed organ pipe.</p><p>The frequency formula in a closed organ pipe is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>405</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>405</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>324</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
